This is correct except for one thing: C. S. Lewis is better known for
writing "That Hideous Strength", "The Chronicles of Narnia", et c.

Lewis Carroll, aka Charles Dodgson, Oxford Mathematician around the turn of
the century, wrote Alice's Adventures in Wonderland and Through The
Looking-Glass (from whence "Jabberwocky").

There's a very nice engraving of the Jabberwocky, by Sir John Tenniel, in
most editions of the book. He doesn't mention it being level 23 though...

